SUMMARY: A Vibrant Afternoon with Dr. Color
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Petaluma Museum for an inspiring afternoon wit
 h Bob Buckter—affectionately known as Dr. Color—a celebrated color consul
 tant whose bold\, imaginative palettes have transformed thousands of Vict
 orian homes and historic buildings in San Francisco and beyond.\n\nThe di
 scussion will be followed by a self-guided walking tour en route to an ex
 clusive reception at one of Petaluma’s most colorful historic residences—
 an opportunity to continue the conversation and experience the power of p
 igment up close.\n\nDr. Color will share stories from his decades-long ca
 reer\, offering insight into his creative approach\, the power of color i
 n shaping how we experience architecture\, and the role of color in histo
 ric preservation. Whether you’re a homeowner\, designer\, preservation en
 thusiast\, or simply curious\, this is a rare opportunity to hear from on
 e of the most influential voices in the field.\n\nPresented by the Petalu
 ma Museum and our Heritage Homes program as part of National Historic Pre
 servation Month\, this event celebrates the importance of preserving and 
 reimagining our shared architectural heritage.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Historic,Architecture,color,victorians
