SUMMARY: Sunday Swing Night at Hall of the Above
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the first Sunday of every month for SUNDAY SWING N
 IGHT at Hall of the Above\n\n🎷 Featuring a new-to-HOTA band\, The doRiaN
  Mode! 🎷\n\nThe doRiaN Mode explores the Great American Songbook as it d
 ishes up vintage jazz\, swinging R&B\, and soulful ballads\, from the sou
 nds of 1920s speakeasies and 1930s big-band swing to 1940s jump blues and
  the rollicking R&B of Ruth Brown. Vocalist and bassist Dorian Bartley le
 ads this Petaluma-based acoustic quartet featuring Robby Elfman on piano/
 clarinet\, Peter Graves on sax\, and Tony Blake on drums. Whether they’re
  stomping at the Savoy in salute to Count Basie or paying homage to R&B l
 egend Etta James\, the doRiaN Mode brings elegance to classic American mu
 sic.\n\n\n💃🏻 Jasmine Worrell\, the Bay Area’s top swing dance instructo
 r\, will offer a class from 4:15 – 5:00\n\n👯 Followed by live music and 
 an open dance floor until 7:00 PM\n\n🎟️ $25 for admission includes the c
 lass — cash at the door. Kids 12 and under are free.\n\n🕺🏾 All skill le
 vels welcome\; no partner required.\n\n\nSee you on the dance floor!
CATEGORIES:Swing-Night,Jazz,Dancing
