SUMMARY: "Paddle The Petaluma: Turn to The River" Guided Kayak Tour
DESCRIPTION:Paddle the Petaluma: Turn to The River is a relaxed\, beginne
 r-friendly guided kayak tour exploring the past\, present\, and future of
  Petaluma’s historic waterway. Launching right from downtown at The Float
 house Petaluma https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org?utm_source=chatgpt.c
 om \, this Sonoma County Signature Experience spends about 90 minutes on 
 the water in stable sit-on-top kayaks\, traveling a gentle mile-and-a-hal
 f route through “Petaluma’s Longest Park.”\n\nAlong the way\, you’ll raft
  up at docks around town\, fascinating landmarks\, and riverfront gatheri
 ng spaces to hear stories about how this Gold Rush-era “saltwater highway
 ” helped shape Petaluma—and how today’s community is continuing to reinve
 nt and reconnect with the river. This isn’t just a history tour. You’ll a
 lso learn about the people\, businesses\, artists\, nonprofits\, and rive
 r advocates helping shape the waterway’s future right now.\n\nEverything 
 is included in the $75 experience: kayak\, gear\, knowledgeable local gui
 des\, insider river stories\, and post-paddle perks at nearby businesses.
  Finish with plenty of time for brunch\, coffee\, shopping\, or simply ha
 nging out downtown by the water. No experience necessary.\n\nNote: The Fl
 oathouse Petaluma is a nonprofit project dedicated to “putting butts in b
 oats and smiles on faces” by offering year-round easy access to the Petal
 uma River in and on people-powered water craft through rentals\, events\,
  classes\, lessons and summer camps.\n\n
CATEGORIES:kayak,Petaluma-River,kayak-tour,paddle-tour
